# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# apps/admin — build-time config for the React admin console.
#
# Vite inlines VITE_* vars into the bundle AT BUILD TIME. They are therefore
# public: anyone can read them in the shipped JS. Never put a password, API key
# or token in this file — the console authenticates at runtime against
# /api/knowledge-hub/login and holds a bearer token in localStorage.
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local overrides (gitignored). On Vercel, set these
# under Project → Settings → Environment Variables instead of committing them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Origin of the bot's Express API.
#
#   Vercel deploy  → REQUIRED. The bot's public HTTPS URL, no trailing slash.
#                    e.g. https://bot.theaurax.in
#   Local dev      → leave EMPTY. `npm run dev` proxies /api to the bot (below).
#   build:express  → leave EMPTY. That build is served by the bot itself, so the
#                    API is already same-origin.
#
# Whatever you set here must also appear in the bot's ADMIN_ALLOWED_ORIGINS
# (as the *console's* origin, not the bot's) or the browser blocks every call.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Dev server only: where `npm run dev` proxies /api and /invoices.
# Defaults to http://localhost:3000. Point it at a deployed bot to work on the
# UI without running the WhatsApp stack locally.
VITE_DEV_API_PROXY=http://localhost:3000
